---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Albuquerque Waxing Guide — ABQWax.ing"
  description="Everything to know about Albuquerque waxing: hard wax vs soft wax, Brazilian, pricing norms, aftercare, and the domain built to own the search. ABQWax.ing is offered at $250,000."
  canonical="/albuquerque-waxing/"
  keywords="Albuquerque waxing, waxing Albuquerque, Albuquerque wax salon, body waxing Albuquerque, waxing near me Albuquerque, ABQWax.ing"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Albuquerque Waxing', path: '/albuquerque-waxing/' },
  ]}
>
  <Header />

  <main class="flex-1">
    <section class="border-b border-ink-100 bg-ink-950">
      <div class="container-narrow py-16 sm:py-24">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-widestx text-gold-400">Albuquerque · Waxing · Guide</p>
        <h1 class="mt-3 max-w-3xl font-display text-4xl font-semibold leading-tight text-white sm:text-6xl">
          Albuquerque waxing, written into the domain
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-100/85 sm:text-lg">
          Waxing is one of the most searched beauty services in the 505. Here is the category, the method, and the name built to hold it — ABQWax<span class="italic text-gold-300">.ing</span>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-padding bg-white">
      <div class="container-narrow grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="lg:col-span-2 space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-800 sm:text-base">
          <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold text-ink-950">Why waxing leads local beauty search</h2>
          <p>
            In Albuquerque, waxing is a recurring purchase, not a one-time splurge. Clients book every three to four weeks,
            which means local search volume is steady all year. The people searching type phrases like
            <strong class="text-ink-950">Albuquerque waxing</strong>, <strong class="text-ink-950">ABQ waxing</strong>, and
            <strong class="text-ink-950">Brazilian wax Albuquerque</strong> — the same words a strong domain should already contain.
          </p>
          <p>
            High-desert heat and a year-round active lifestyle keep smoothness a practical, in-demand service rather than a
            seasonal luxury. From legs and brows to full Brazilian and hard-wax treatments for sensitive areas, the category
            spans a wide menu with loyal repeat clients.
          </p>
          <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold text-ink-950">What makes a name own the search</h2>
          <p>
            Most salons compete on ads and listings. A domain that reads as the exact query — <strong class="text-ink-950">ABQ waxing</strong> —
            shortens the path from search to click to booking. The city code, the category, and the service verb live in a single hostname,
            leaving less room for a competitor to intercept the same phrase.
          </p>
          <p>
            Read <a href="/hard-wax-albuquerque/" class="font-medium text-gold-500 underline-offset-4 hover:underline">our hard wax breakdown</a>,
            or the <a href="/brazilian-wax-albuquerque/" class="font-medium text-gold-500 underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Brazilian wax Albuquerque guide</a>
            for the specifics of each service.
          </p>
        </div>
        <aside class="rounded-3xl border border-ink-100 bg-ink-50 p-6 sm:p-8">
          <p class="text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-widestx text-gold-500">The domain</p>
          <p class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl font-semibold text-ink-950">ABQWax.ing</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-700">Read aloud, it is Albuquerque waxing. Typed into a browser, it is the listing they meant to find.</p>
          <p class="mt-4 font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-gold-500">$250,000</p>
          <a href="#acquisition" class="btn-primary mt-4">Request terms</a>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-padding bg-ink-50">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold text-ink-950 sm:text-4xl">Common questions about waxing in Albuquerque</h2>
        <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <article class="card">
            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink-950">How long does a wax last?</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-700">Three to four weeks on average. Hair is removed from the root, so regrowth is soft and gradual rather than stubbly.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink-950">Hard wax or soft wax?</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-700">Hard wax grips hair, not skin, so it is preferred for Brazilian, bikini, and underarm work. Soft wax is faster for large areas like legs.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink-950">How long should hair be?</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-700">About a quarter to half an inch — roughly two to three weeks of growth — for the wax to grip cleanly.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink-950">What is the best schedule?</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-700">Every four weeks keeps the cycle consistent and makes each session faster and more comfortable over time.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
